### 6. Trade‑off Comparison

| Aspect | Outbox | Saga |
|--------|--------|------|
| Consistency | Strong at write time | Eventual, requires compensation |
| Latency | Single request, minimal extra hops | Multiple round‑trips, higher latency |
| Failure handling | Lost‑event risk mitigated by outbox | Explicit compensation logic, more code |
| Complexity | Simple CRUD + polling | Orchestrator logic, state machine |
| Scalability | Publisher can be scaled independently | Orchestrator is a bottleneck unless sharded |

The saga pattern excels when domain boundaries are clear and compensating actions are well‑defined. It trades immediate consistency for greater flexibility in distributed environments, making it a natural complement to the outbox when the business requires a higher level of coordination across services.

